#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059508 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a10cafc6-9da7-5ffc-a0c7-686a7638fbd9" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 2x2 Augmented Matrix to REF Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/id #uuid "0a9e6824-677a-5fae-9867-1701e7d8378f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4697" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -8\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nM\\begin{vmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -8\\end{bmatrix} & R_{2}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{2} + (-3)R_{1}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -8\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{2} \\mid:=-\\frac{1}{8}R_{2}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\nx + 2y = 0; y = 1\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=1$ tells us the value of $y$. Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+2(1)=0 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x=-2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=1$. Or, in vector form,\n\n$$\n\\left< -2,1 \\right>\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059509 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07abc1cc-5794-51a6-bad4-40565eae52be" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/id #uuid "1eea81be-26d7-57dd-a622-d66300de7f4f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4698" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n$-x + 5y = 5; x - 6y = 5$.\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nM\\begin{vmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & R_{1}\\end{vmatrix}:=-R_{1}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{2} &:=R_{2} + (-1)R_{1} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 10\\end{bmatrix} & R_{2}\\end{vmatrix}:=-R_{2}; ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\nx - 5y =-5; y =-10\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-10$ tells us the value of $y$. Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-5(-10)=-5 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x=-55\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-55$ and $y=-10$. Or, in vector form, $\\langle -55,-10 \\rangle$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059895 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07abc1cc-5794-51a6-bad4-40565eae52be" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1faa74d-9eec-582e-b43e-bf73022143fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$,\n$x =-4$ and $y = 1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056091} {:answer/id #uuid "ea80ffec-99ef-5f1e-adbd-1a0b5c26333a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$,\n$x =-4$ and $y = 1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056092} {:answer/id #uuid "0dc62860-253d-526a-a46f-3c4e1d9f320b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$,\n$x =-2$ and $y = 2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056093} {:answer/id #uuid "5b309705-5ccd-578d-8cbf-a61e0a123496" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$,\n$x =-8$ and $y = 2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056094} {:answer/id #uuid "70f90bb5-57b9-5197-b1ce-e2b87